      "artist": "FaceMePLS from The Hague, The Netherlands",
      "description": "Kamp Vught was een van de vijf concentratiekampen in Nederland tijdens de Tweede Wereldoorlog. De bouw van het kamp werd in 1942 gestart. In totaal werden er ruim 31.000 mensen in het kamp gedetineerd, waaronder twaalfduizend Joden.\nHerzogenbusch concentration camp (kamp Vught) was a Nazi concentration camp located in Vught near the city of 's-Hertogenbosch, in the Netherlands. Herzogenbusch was the only concentration camp run directly by SS in western Europe outside of Germany. The camp was first used in 1943 and held 31,000 prisoners. 749 prisoners died in the camp. The others were transferred to other camps shortly before the camp was liberated by the Allied Forces in 1944. After the war the camp was used as a prison for Germans. Now there is a visitors center with exhibitions and a national monument remembering the camp and its victims.\n\nBron Wikipedia.",
